  "education": {
    "pathophysiology": "Type II Diabetes Mellitus is a metabolic disease characterized by chronic hyperglycemia resulting from insulin resistance combined with insufficient compensatory insulin secretion. Over time, high glucose causes non-enzymatic glycation of arterial walls, resulting in endothelial damage, peripheral neuropathy, glomerulosclerosis (renal damage), and accelerated coronary artery atherosclerosis.",
    "links": ["Pancreas", "Kidney", "Heart", "Brain"]
